{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "An Emotional Week"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Let's Work It Out"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le04ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What Clauses and Long Noun Phrases as Subjects"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You shift emphasis from the beginning to another part of the sentence by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> and <span class=\"italic\">who</span> phrases as subjects."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Usually, you focus on the person doing the action in this case, the comedian telling jokes. <br/>   Example: <span class=\"italic\">John told a funny joke.</span><br/><br/> If we wish to place emphasis on another part of the sentence, we isolate that part and package up the rest of the information into a <span class=\"italic\">what</span>-phrase (or sometimes a <span class=\"italic\">that</span>-clause.)<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">What John said was funny."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">That</span> with a subordinated content clause can function as the subject of a sentence.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">That he imitated our teacher was funny.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">What</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Who</span> serves as a placeholder for the content of the noun phrase that has been moved to the end of the sentence. The effect is that more emphasis is placed on the initial content.<br/> Example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">What was hilarious was his imitation of the teacher.</span><br/>        <span class=\"italic\"> Who he should have made fun of was the principal."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What was especially provocative was how it can be applied at work."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Who you really need to apply it to is your boss! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "That I've been confused by her behavior isn't really surprising. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Who you should focus on changing a bit is you. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Tag Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use tag questions to ask for clarification and confirmation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Question tags are short questions at the end of statements. They are mainly used in speech when we want to:<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">confirm that something is true or not</span>, or</li> <li><span class=\"strong\">to encourage a reply</span> from the person we are speaking to.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018yes'.<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A negative statement is followed by a positive question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018no'.<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were</span> you? </li> <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal</span> verb, the tag will be the same.<br/> For all other main verbs, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do/does</span> or <span class=\"italic\">did/didn't</span>.<br/><br/> Look at the examples in the chart:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":12,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't/was't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"wont you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's really interesting information, isn't it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You are going to use some of the EI strategies to improve your relationship with her, aren't you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's the key, isn't it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's been my problem, hasn't it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It sounds so easy, doesn't it? "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "compelling"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very interesting; able to capture and hold your attention"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The novel was really compelling!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about reactions and behavior in different situations."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "provocative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "causing discussion, thought, argument, etc."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What was especially provocative was how it can be applied at work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "I can't wait"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to express anticipation or excitement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can't wait until the weekend!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to implement"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to begin to do or use (something, such as a plan)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'm excited to implement some of what I learned about EI. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to gauge"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to measure or to estimate"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'll be better able to gauge her behavior and where it's coming from. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "conduct "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way that a person behaves in a particular place or situation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I haven't looked for the reasons behind her conduct. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cognizant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "aware of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to work on being more cognizant of other people's emotions and reactions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think about the 5 categories of Emotional Intelligence: self-awareness, self-regulation, motivation, empathy, social skills."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, write survey questions to find out how much emotional intelligence your classmates have."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 10-12 questions to ask how emotionally intelligent people think they are."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask your questions to 3 people."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your findings to your class or group."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about reactions and behavior."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I shift emphasis by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">that</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask for clarification and confirmation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write and conduct a survey."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about reactions and behavior."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can shift emphasis by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">that</span>."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can ask for clarification and confirmation."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What are some things you would like to improve about the way you communicate?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "In which situations is it better to share your emotions, and when is it better to keep them to yourself? "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Relationships can be difficult, can't they?"}]}, {"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "STI", "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Vanessa helps Sally find <span class=\"t